{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/the-crossroads-continent/1546043-inktober-postings-and-story-with-art-redux-3","id":1546043,"title":"Inktober postings and story with art Redux #3","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Crossroads Continent"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-17T13:39:02-08:00","id":1546043,"title":"Inktober postings and story with art Redux #3","content":"Inktober Redux3: Having broken through the ancient sealed secret door, our adventurers worked their way through a series of trapped corridors, detecting and defusing - or not detecting and springing - them. They entered a room that was perhaps some sort of jail or torture room, or both, and Corsika, using all of her considerable strength, pulled a long, single-edged, sword out of the wall where it had impaled a human skeleton - holding the remains in place for centuries. Pushing open doors at the end of the room revealed a much larger chamber filled with the detritus of centuries, mold and moss covered - stepping in, their feet sank through the slippery debris to their shins and knees.<br /> <br /> At this point, they were very much surprised to be hailed _from behind_ as an armored dwarf entered the torture room. (So, this is how a new player character named Asmodeus joined the group for the night, as one of my veteran players was in town and asked to play. Fill-in characters was always something we did, and I figured we'd continue the practice).<br /> <br /> He seemed OK to the gang, so all of them started going deeper into the large chamber, which had the feel of once having been a ritual chamber of some kind. From beneath the debris rose multiple skeletons in ancient, strange armor, a swelling under the debris from the far side of the chamber began moving towards them, and an unnatural vortex of wind began swirling some fifteen feet up in the center of the room, buffeting the PCs with pieces of debris.<br /> <br /> As the party split up to attack the skeletons, the hump of debris burst open to reveal a giant skeleton also in rusting, ancient armor of odd design, and Asmodeus the dwarf warrior immediately flung a hand axe at it and braced for it's attack - leaving the rest of the group to deal with the normal-sized skeletons, and... the apparition that appeared in the swirling vortex! A terrifying ghostly presence that radiated evil it began cackling in an unknown language and it's mask began to glow.<br /> <br /> Several arrows were fired at the creature, which seemed unfazed, and as Corsika prepared to hurl her trident, a voice in her head begged her to allow it to inhabit her form to fight the masked undead creature hovering above them. Later, she said it didn't actually speak, but she could feel its intent and desire for vengeance on the apparition - a necromancer from ancient times - and that was good enough for her! The spirit joined her and raised them both into the air to attack the necromancer with her new-found sword. Seeing the threat, the thing summoned a similar kind of sword of purest dark energy and the two blades clashed into each other.<br /> <br /> (So, fighting was going on, attacks and damage rolls were being made, and at each of Corsika's turns I tried a bit of cinematic storytelling by having her have visions of the spirit that was helping her. A warrior betrayed by the high priest necromancer, and his beloved tortured and changing to an undead creature in the torture room. The warrior drove his katana into her to spare her from an undead existence, striking with such passion that he buried his sword in the wall, who then went out to the larger chamber and struck down as many of the guards as he could before killing the mortal form of the necromancer - who transformed into the undead spirit and slew the warrior, leaving them all trapped in the chamber and the warrior's spirit within his blade. I think the little break away stories were enjoyed by the gang and it added some pathos to the event.)<br /> <br /> Knowing the story, Corsika and the other's fought hard, defeated the necromancer and his minions, saw the warrior and his wife reunited as spirits who could now go into their afterlife together, and recovered a bunch of gems and other valuable things. They would return to their boat and work their way out of the sea caves, head up the coast to another city, sell stuff, buy stuff like Corsika's new boots, Asmodeus would go on his way, they'd get some more info, and steal the were-rat smuggler's bigger boat from the docks so now they had two: a veritable pirate fleet!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}